Z||000000||frankshel||09-01-2001||10:08 PM||||I went to the car parts store and asked for a tachometer filter for my 85 2.5 Fiero and they did not know what it was or what I was talking about. Is ther another name for it or is it a Dealer item only? Someone please let me know.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Frank Sheldon<BR>Ticonderoga, NY||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||09-01-2001||10:32 PM||||I do believe that the tach filter is for v6 engines only.  Atleast in the 88 manual it is.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||09-01-2001||10:59 PM||||I've never paid any attention to my 2.5, but pretty sure it has a tach filter. Maybe I'm wrong, I had a shop do the rebuild and install in June, shoulda went down and took a good look while the eng was out. BUT, the Haynes manual shows a tach filter in the diagram for the "efi,ign,service eng soon light,tachometer"section. Page 276.Try a search--tach filter--tech archives--any date--subj only. Lots of answers there<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||09-02-2001||11:23 AM||||Every Fiero has a tach filter. And I don't believe they're made anymore.<P>About your only options are Rodney Dickman, making your own (instructions are in the Archive) or scoping out other GM cars with tachs and looking for the filter (I'll bet they're all the same).||||reg||1
Z||000004||William Federle||09-02-2001||12:42 PM||||I have 1 1984 Fiero SE and I know it has a tach filter because the ground wire came off of it and the tach went crazy. It was located on the left side of the engine in a wire bundle. One wire goes to the coil, one goes to the tach, and a ground wire is soldered to the case. <P>My ground wire came off. I soldered a new wire to the case and connected it to the engine block, and my problem was solved.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||09-02-2001||12:43 PM||||I've been to the parts store before and asked the same question, and got the same response. I think they're discontinued. Rodney Dickman sells a replacement. Or make a post in the mall. And yes, the 2.5 has them, at least my 86 does.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||1
